# oracle: pair_style body/rounded/polyhedron between a rounded cube and a sphere body (one sub-particle, the sphere-polyhedron route), friction mu 0.3, approach speed 2 with lateral sliding, fix nve/body, 2000 steps: thermo pe ke etotal press and the atom state
# Measured with native LAMMPS: thermo max relative error 3.7e-11, per-atom state (x, v, f) max 4.5e-15 (5.1e-12 and 1.0e-14 before fix nve/body used the port of MathExtra::richardson: the remaining last-bit differences of the contact dynamics grow differently). The sphere is a body with one sub-particle (zero moments of inertia), so the sphere-polyhedron route (sphere_against_polyhedron) is exercised with friction mu 0.3.
# oracle-inputs: w121body_cube_sphere.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-12
units           lj
dimension       3
atom_style      body rounded/polyhedron 1 8
atom_modify     map array
read_data       w121body_cube_sphere.data
set             atom 1 vx 2.0 vy 0.5 vz 0.0
set             atom 2 vx -2.0 vy 0.0 vz 0.0
pair_style      body/rounded/polyhedron 20 5 0.3 1 0.5
pair_coeff      * * 100 1
comm_modify     vel yes
neighbor        0.5 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
timestep        0.001
fix             1 all nve/body
thermo_style    custom step pe ke etotal press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          50
run             2000
